00:31:49.110 --> 00:31:50.790
Yo, ho, ho, it's 110.

00:31:52.770 --> 00:31:54.010
My face is melting.

00:31:54.650 --> 00:31:56.030
Thank you so much for being here.

00:31:56.130 --> 00:31:56.890
I'm happy to be here.

00:31:56.910 --> 00:31:58.270
And you guys are gonna perform on the show.

00:31:58.290 --> 00:31:59.450
We're very excited about that.

00:31:59.510 --> 00:31:59.710
I am.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:00.720
I just want to mention something.

00:32:00.840 --> 00:32:01.860
I have seen you perform.

00:32:02.060 --> 00:32:03.860
Over the years, I would go to different benefits.

00:32:04.200 --> 00:32:05.100
You're very kind.

00:32:05.100 --> 00:32:09.840
You show up at a lot of the benefits in New York that I've attended, and you always perform at them.

00:32:09.920 --> 00:32:12.460
And you're just fantastic with an audience.

00:32:12.800 --> 00:32:15.820
You really do lock in with an audience right away.

00:32:15.920 --> 00:32:17.340
And you've given it a lot of thought.

00:32:17.420 --> 00:32:19.520
What is your strategy when you work a crowd?

00:32:20.160 --> 00:32:23.440
Well, I mean, there's a little bit of a seduction that's involved.

00:32:23.600 --> 00:32:29.050
You know, you have to try to get in there and work intimately with that audience.

00:32:29.050 --> 00:32:29.930
I mean, it's...

00:32:30.480 --> 00:32:32.880
It's a craft, it's something that you learn how to do.

00:32:33.600 --> 00:32:36.400
You should try sometime to get intimidating.

00:32:44.230 --> 00:32:45.170
It's not easy to do.

00:32:45.310 --> 00:32:46.920
I mean, it'd be hard with that guy

00:32:46.920 --> 00:32:48.300
with the lightning bolt on his shirt,

00:32:48.420 --> 00:32:49.700
but the girl over here would be cute,

00:32:49.820 --> 00:32:50.740
that would be easier, you know?

00:32:51.400 --> 00:32:54.920
I like the guy, seems cool, yeah.

00:32:57.880 --> 00:32:58.520
Settle down.

00:33:02.980 --> 00:33:04.980
So you think I'd come out during the monologue

00:33:05.380 --> 00:33:07.220
and really try and seduce them

00:33:07.220 --> 00:33:09.860
and make it a sexual dance, as it were.

00:33:10.870 --> 00:33:11.950
You're a snake charmer.

00:33:12.070 --> 00:33:14.190
Look, you could think of it, grab a mic stand,

00:33:14.310 --> 00:33:15.150
you know, just go out there

00:33:15.150 --> 00:33:17.150
and work the crowd a little more intimately.

00:33:17.330 --> 00:33:18.350
I watch you, you're back here,

00:33:18.410 --> 00:33:19.870
you're reserved, you're keeping a distance.

00:33:20.410 --> 00:33:21.810
You gotta get a lady,

00:33:21.930 --> 00:33:23.250
you gotta grab the lady by the hand,

00:33:23.830 --> 00:33:25.200
you have to know how to, you know.

00:33:25.460 --> 00:33:27.840
You gotta know how to do these things.

00:33:27.960 --> 00:33:29.580
It seems to me that you're...

00:33:29.580 --> 00:33:29.960
I'm trying...

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.220
I did that with Ava before in A.

00:33:31.280 --> 00:33:32.740
I got slapped real hard.

00:33:34.680 --> 00:33:36.120
It's different for you, John.

00:33:36.360 --> 00:33:39.280
That ad is out my bedroom window.

00:33:39.500 --> 00:33:40.360
Yeah, is it really?

00:33:40.520 --> 00:33:41.260
I swear to goodness gracious.

00:33:41.260 --> 00:33:43.160
Were you the one writing against it?

00:33:43.220 --> 00:33:44.140
No, I appreciate it.

00:33:44.240 --> 00:33:44.600
Yeah, yeah.

00:33:45.180 --> 00:33:47.340
That is out my bedroom window.

00:33:47.800 --> 00:33:49.220
Do you even leave the house?

00:33:49.440 --> 00:33:50.140
I would just be.

00:33:50.520 --> 00:33:51.160
You know, they were saying,

00:33:51.320 --> 00:33:52.400
some are complaining about it.

00:33:52.500 --> 00:33:53.560
I'm like looking out the window.

00:33:53.820 --> 00:33:54.980
This is working for me.

00:33:55.060 --> 00:33:56.480
Yeah, very nice, very nice.

00:33:56.500 --> 00:33:57.180
Ava Mendes is big.

00:33:57.460 --> 00:33:59.300
Let me ask you about something.

00:33:59.300 --> 00:33:59.960
I heard a rumor.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:06.340
that you had a Labor Day party at your home.

00:34:07.010 --> 00:34:09.190
And I think this may have been out at the beach.

00:34:09.310 --> 00:34:09.910
Is that correct?

00:34:10.330 --> 00:34:13.550
And you had a couple of friends over who were also musicians,

00:34:13.550 --> 00:34:18.340
and it turned into the greatest supergroup jam of all time.

00:34:18.400 --> 00:34:21.120
And it's been discussed, but it has not been verified for me.

00:34:21.330 --> 00:34:22.990
Who jumped up on stage?

00:34:23.640 --> 00:34:27.320
Paul McCartney, Billy Joel, Jimmy Buffett, Roger Waters, me,

00:34:27.940 --> 00:34:29.300
and Springsteen was there.

00:34:30.760 --> 00:34:42.420
Did anybody think to record this or shoot tape or anything?

00:34:43.010 --> 00:34:46.970
No, I was having a barbecue, and all these guys were there.

00:34:47.610 --> 00:34:51.130
I know this sounds really, I'm sorry, folks, but it is true.

00:34:51.550 --> 00:34:53.920
And literally, Academy Award winners...

00:34:53.920 --> 00:34:55.340
I have barbecues like that. I'm not blown away by this.

00:34:56.430 --> 00:34:59.110
I've had barbecues where it's Pauly Shore and me.

00:35:01.020 --> 00:35:01.740
Carrot Top.

00:35:01.980 --> 00:35:03.160
And then we all get on stage.

00:35:05.980 --> 00:35:06.340
Yeah.

00:35:06.580 --> 00:35:08.600
I'm sorry, Andy, I was gonna invite you, but you know.

00:35:09.360 --> 00:35:10.380
Trust me, it's okay.

00:35:14.990 --> 00:35:16.730
So anyway, you all get on stage.

00:35:16.890 --> 00:35:18.590
Do you even remember what you guys sang?

00:35:18.870 --> 00:35:19.030
Not really.

00:35:19.170 --> 00:35:20.970
I mean, probably Beatles, Stones, Chuck Berry.

00:35:21.090 --> 00:35:21.990
You know, things that you know,

00:35:22.070 --> 00:35:23.130
because everybody was there.

00:35:23.330 --> 00:35:25.480
But all these guys were there,

00:35:25.660 --> 00:35:27.980
and I just did one of those with the house band,

00:35:28.120 --> 00:35:29.700
and you know, a bunch of guys, you know, like the guys.

00:35:30.320 --> 00:35:32.200
In the band here, old friends of ours from Jersey.

00:35:32.420 --> 00:35:34.660
But anyhow, you look up and you go, anybody want to play?

00:35:34.740 --> 00:35:36.460
And then you look up and they were all there already.

00:35:36.640 --> 00:35:37.620
They'd all grab the instruments.

00:35:37.940 --> 00:35:43.090
So right in the backyard, Academy Award winners were like breaking through the hedges to get on.

00:35:43.150 --> 00:35:45.330
People were coming from miles around just to see this happen.

00:35:45.470 --> 00:35:45.610
Yeah.

00:35:45.790 --> 00:35:45.990
Yeah.

00:35:45.990 --> 00:35:48.450
It was just a beach party that turned into something amazing.

00:35:48.590 --> 00:35:49.470
That'll never happen again.

00:35:49.470 --> 00:35:52.580
We barely got any pictures of it because it was just spontaneous.

00:35:52.860 --> 00:35:53.040
That's very.

00:35:53.160 --> 00:35:55.560
And in a way, it's kind of cool that no one recorded it or took a picture.

00:35:55.620 --> 00:35:56.860
I think it's great that it just happened.

00:35:56.980 --> 00:35:59.360
It was just a barbecued backyard.

00:35:59.720 --> 00:35:59.980
Let me.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.440
Let me ask you about something.

00:36:01.640 --> 00:36:04.040
You are, you guys are NBC artists in residence.

00:36:04.200 --> 00:36:04.560
Is that right?

00:36:04.600 --> 00:36:05.100
That's true.

00:36:05.340 --> 00:36:07.120
And I don't quite know what that means.

00:36:07.220 --> 00:36:09.460
It means that in a way you kind of belong to NBC

00:36:09.940 --> 00:36:10.920
for a period of time.

00:36:11.040 --> 00:36:11.320
Is that right?

00:36:11.420 --> 00:36:14.720
I like to refer to it as Jeff Zucker's indentured servitude.

00:36:15.060 --> 00:36:16.000
Yeah, yeah.

00:36:16.400 --> 00:36:17.340
I know what that's like.

00:36:17.340 --> 00:36:19.120
I've been here since 10 o'clock this morning.

00:36:19.360 --> 00:36:21.640
You guys have me back there slicing fruit.

00:36:22.340 --> 00:36:24.960
I got here before half the band got here this morning.

00:36:25.140 --> 00:36:27.500
Yeah, you guys, they put you guys to work.

00:36:27.580 --> 00:36:29.180
They have you guys literally doing everything.

00:36:29.180 --> 00:36:29.520
Everything.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.220
Everything, parking cars, seating, some of the car signals.

00:36:37.520 --> 00:36:40.240
Hey, yo, Conan, I got your dry cleaning right here.

00:36:40.340 --> 00:36:40.800
What do you want me to do?

00:36:41.060 --> 00:36:42.380
That's great, just put it up in my office,

00:36:42.440 --> 00:36:44.260
and if you could wash my dog as well, that'd be great.

00:36:44.700 --> 00:36:46.320
Thank you very much, Richie Sembor, everybody.

00:36:52.940 --> 00:36:54.500
I mean, we're still, whatever it takes.

00:36:54.520 --> 00:36:56.700
He makes that suit look good, I gotta tell you.

00:36:57.000 --> 00:36:57.860
He looks good in polyester.

00:36:57.860 --> 00:36:59.820
I've never seen a page look that cool.

00:37:01.690 --> 00:37:03.690
Very quickly, we are pretty much out of time.

00:37:03.710 --> 00:37:05.770
I wanted to do one thing, which is we found out today,

00:37:05.930 --> 00:37:07.950
I never knew this about you, it's a great revelation

00:37:07.950 --> 00:37:10.430
that in high school, you were a bit of a band geek.

00:37:10.610 --> 00:37:11.050
Is that right?

00:37:11.880 --> 00:37:15.140
Well, yeah, I was a trumpet player for five minutes.

00:37:15.140 --> 00:37:16.920
Not Mark Pender, but I humbled him.

00:37:16.920 --> 00:37:18.580
You were in the marching band and you played?

00:37:19.150 --> 00:37:19.870
You were?

00:37:20.170 --> 00:37:20.530
Drill team.

00:37:20.690 --> 00:37:21.790
Drill team dork, yeah.

00:37:21.890 --> 00:37:22.310
I don't get slapped.

00:37:24.370 --> 00:37:25.690
Oh, how do you do it?

00:37:27.430 --> 00:37:29.970
Well, we found a picture of you from high school.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:32.460
I just had to put this up because, yeah, well, I just, uh,

00:37:33.320 --> 00:37:33.640
twerk.

00:37:33.800 --> 00:37:37.790
I just love the hair.

00:37:40.080 --> 00:37:43.460
The circle is in stores now.

00:37:43.660 --> 00:37:44.160
And this thing is-

00:37:44.160 --> 00:37:45.080
The number one record in America?

00:37:45.200 --> 00:37:46.380
The number one record in America.

00:37:46.760 --> 00:37:47.100
The circle.

00:37:47.340 --> 00:37:49.260
And you're going to come back and play for us.

00:37:49.320 --> 00:37:49.460
Yes.

00:37:49.730 --> 00:37:51.090
Stick around. You don't want to miss that.

00:37:51.290 --> 00:37:52.310
Jon Bon Jovi, everybody.

00:37:52.470 --> 00:37:52.730
We'll be right back.

00:38:00.600 --> 00:38:10.750
We're here with a song from their brand new album, The Circle.

00:38:11.050 --> 00:38:15.030
And on February 19th, they'll kick off a big North American tour in Seattle, Washington.

00:38:15.070 --> 00:38:17.050
Please welcome Bon Jovi.

00:38:36.300 --> 00:38:43.800
some miracles this one goes out to the ones in need this one goes out in a

00:38:43.800 --> 00:38:45.780
little cynical saying

00:39:01.440 --> 00:39:01.800
Don't hear it.

00:40:00.220 --> 00:40:00.380
Thank you.

00:40:31.050 --> 00:40:31.370
I

00:40:45.670 --> 00:40:45.810
Yeah.

00:41:30.160 --> 00:41:30.400
We.

00:42:32.910 --> 00:42:33.490
Thank you so much.

00:42:35.990 --> 00:42:36.430
That's our show.

00:42:36.530 --> 00:42:37.290
I want to thank all my guests.

00:42:37.370 --> 00:42:38.470
Thank you for Late Night with Jimmy Fallon.

00:42:38.550 --> 00:42:38.890
Bye, everybody.

00:42:39.050 --> 00:42:39.170
Bye.
